<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jama Masjid, Burhanpur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1590">1590</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jama Masjid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a> is the congregational mosque of Burhanpur in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, completed in 1590 under Raja Ali Khan, the Faruqi sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandesh">Khandesh</a> also known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> IV. Built of black stone with two tall minarets, it carries inscriptions in Arabic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a>, an unusual combination, and is one of the finest buildings of the Faruqi period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jama-masjid-burhanpur.jpg" alt="Jama Masjid, Burhanpur" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Cousens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jama_Masjid_at_Burhanpur,_photographed_by_Henry_Cousens_in_the_19th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
